   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Bomb_%28Buckcherry_album%29",
   "resumo_en": "Time Bomb is the second studio album by American rock band Buckcherry. It was produced by John Travis  and released on March 27, 2001, by DreamWorks Records. It is the band's only album to feature Yogi Lonich on rhythm guitar and is the final album to feature the original lineup, as bassist Jonathan Brightman and drummer Devon Glenn both left the band in August 2001 and January 2002, respectively. It is also Buckcherry's last album before a three-year hiatus, which lasted from 2002 to 2005."
